<crash-analysis>
The memory leak occurs in the `CleanSpaces` function within the `tidy-html5` library. A `Stack` object is allocated at the beginning of the function, but it seems that under certain conditions, it is not deallocated by the corresponding `TY_(freeStack)` call at the end of the function. This is a bug in the `tidy-html5` library, as it should be able to handle any input without leaking memory.

The fuzz driver is using the `tidy-html5` library correctly. It creates a `TidyDoc`, parses input from a temporary file, and then releases the `TidyDoc`. This is the standard and recommended way to use the library. There are no issues with the fuzz driver's logic.

The bug is in the `CleanSpaces` function. The loop that processes nodes might have a logic error that causes the function to exit prematurely without freeing the stack, or there might be an issue with how the stack is used that leads to a leak. A thorough review of the `CleanSpaces` function's logic is needed to identify the exact cause of the leak and apply a fix.
</crash-analysis>

